    Input: rmi4 - sequence an in-cell I2C touchscreen with its panel
    
    An in-cell controller may stop answering I2C requests while its display
    panel is off. Register an optional DRM panel follower so the controller
    sleeps before panel unprepare and resumes after panel prepare. System
    sleep defers to these callbacks for a follower.
    
    Track regulator enable references through common power helpers, including
    runtime callbacks and cleanup. Runtime callbacks also defer to a followed
    panel. Keep existing warning-only handling of runtime function-resume
    errors while preserving regulator-enable errors. The current RMI driver
    does not enable runtime PM; synthetic callback controls verify consistent
    tracking if these callbacks are used.
    
    Retain devres ordering: unregister the follower before unregistering the
    RMI transport, then release supplies while the reset descriptor is valid.
    Assert reset before releasing supplies, including failed-probe cleanup.
    
    Adapt Timothy Schmidt's original panel change 5a30fcb447dd and reset
    cleanup 7297314a644f. Preserve their authorship and the panel change's
    Claude assistance attribution. Host ASan/UBSan tests exercise extracted
    callbacks with mocked I/O; no current-base hardware test is claimed.
    
    Original AI assistance used Claude:claude-opus-5-5 with checkpatch.
    Codex:GPT-6 assisted this current-tree adaptation and source-extracted
    ASan/UBSan qualification. The task was to preserve the original hardware
    description and sequencing while checking current APIs and error paths.

